Subject: [PATCH 2/3] R80b, part 1, patch 2 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M14; Review 80, the SM seat's finding 29, which main checked and found held):
 THE LOCK OF B1861 ASKS THAT THE PLAN'S PAGE QUOTE NOTHING OF THE OWNER, BY
 SHAPE AND NOT BY ONE SPELLING.

WHAT STOOD. Two lines at the end of a test about another matter: one phrase had to be on the page, and one spelling of a quotation had to be absent. They passed while the page held a block quotation of the owner.

WHAT IS CHANGED. A reader of the page, what_the_plans_page_quotes, with a test of its own. It reports three shapes: a block quotation, of which the page has none of its own; a quotation mark that opens with a word for the owner in the 120 characters before it, in the same cell; an account that the source keeps in plain words, printed inside quotation marks. The two old lines stand in a dated note where they were.

THE PLANTED CASES, in the patch's own test: eight pages, each of which passes what the lock asked before and is reported now. The first is the page as the builder printed it until the patch before this one. Three twins stay quiet: a seat's sentence that names the owner, quoted in its cell; a possessive; a question of main's with the option chosen. Run on the page of the commit before patch 1, the reader reports the block quotation at line 980, and the old two lines pass.

WHAT THE READER FOUND AND DID NOT MEND: a ruling of 2026-10-08 that the page names by three words in single marks, in two places (the package WP-1.4 and its row in section 9). Whether a ruling's name in marks is a quotation of the owner is main's to say. The two are held by name in the lock, counted, so that a third is reported; the table shortens freely.

WHAT IT CANNOT SEE, said in its docstring: his words given with no mark at all, or set in italics.

The lock passes: 19 tests. 0 of 19.
